{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed for review as Gerrit change 1437 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1437).\n\nDispositions, one per workflow that ran on a push to main:\n- test.yml / optionality.yml / verify-identity.yml — main added to push.branches-ignore; 6-hourly schedules at minutes 41/47/53. Non-main push CI preserved.\n- prompt-eval.yml — main added to push.branches-ignore; weekly live-tier cron untouched.\n- codeql.yml — push key dropped entirely; weekly security scan kept; workflow_dispatch added (it had none).\n- terraform-drift.yml — push key dropped entirely; daily drift sweep kept.\nUntouched by instruction: gerrit-verify.yaml, both reconcilers, external-integration.yml, mirror-guard.yml, and all four workflow_call reusables — proven by the diff, which lists none of them.\n\ntest.yml also gains a caller-level main-health-report job (schedule/dispatch only, if: always()) that resolves the last known-green SHA from the Actions API and renders the bisect recipe. Both the lookup and the rendering live in scripts/main_health_report.py with the gh call injected as a Runner, so the failure modes are unit-tested. The job is added to check_verify_gate_parity.py EXCLUDED_JOBS and to the workflow-parity test's intentional-asymmetry set, because it gates nothing and has no Verified-lane counterpart.\n\nLocal gates green: make lint, make typecheck, make config-check, the Verified-gate parity script, and the full CI pytest invocation. One unrelated pre-existing local failure in tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py (grounding backend availability) is untouched by this change.\n\nPlan-review attestation was earned only after working around ticket 895c-3eb2-043a-4de1: the Bedrock grammar-compilation failure on the standard model class. Running with REBAR_LLM_STANDARD_MODEL pointed at opus-4-8 let the verification pass complete, which then produced a real blocking finding (the actions: read + GH_TOKEN precondition for the run-history lookup) that four earlier INDETERMINATE runs had never surfaced."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785957876084015001,"uuid":"9a2439ff-17b6-4fe7-9702-e5d4d80182c9"}